{
  "id": "minimax-h3-fasth3-pack",
  "name": "Community — MiniMax H3 (FastH3 8-Step V2)",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "author": "FastVideo (hao-ai-lab); Comfy-Org repack",
  "nsfw": false,
  "description": "FastVideo's FastH3 8-Step V2: a data-free DMD2 distillation of MiniMax H3 trained with VSA block-sparse attention at 80% sparsity, so it generates video and stereo audio in eight transformer forwards with no classifier-free guidance. This is the Comfy-Org repack of the distilled checkpoint (20.6 GB int8 ConvRot, a separate download from the base H3 weights) with the official ComfyUI template graph: sigma shift 10/3, comfy-kitchen attention backend, VSA keep 10%. REQUIRES SimpliGen engine 0.36 or later (the block-sparse attention node); on older engines every card shows as needing repair. SimpliGen's own SageAttention and Sol-Attn injection are switched off for these cards because VSA is the attention pattern the weights were trained on; the wiki notes sol-attn and sla are not compatible with this checkpoint. Text and image to video only: FL2VA first/last-frame conditioning is supported, Ref2VA was not distilled. BAKE 2026-09-16 on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti, engine 0.36.0, 5 s at 480p, same seeds and prompts as the TaoMate 3-Step and Turbo Accelerated (10-step) packs: sharper on every scene (Laplacian talking head 68 vs 46 vs 29, product 257 vs 111 vs 121, beach run 138 vs 58 vs 102) and it keeps real motion on the run (frame-to-frame energy 6.7 against the turbo pack's 7.2, where TaoMate drops to 4.5). Dialogue verbatim with the mouth closing on the last word; image-to-video kept the presenter and studio from the still. About 80 s per five-second shot, the same wall as the 10-step turbo. FastVideo's own card warns difficult motion, fine detail and some audio may remain below the base model; three seeds did not show it, but it is three seeds. Shares the text encoder and VAEs with the MiniMax H3 pack.",
  "tags": [
    "8-Step",
    "Distill",
    "FastVideo",
    "I2V",
    "Local",
    "MiniMax H3",
    "T2V",
    "VSA",
    "Video"
  ],
